{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. Johnson, I'm Dr. Patel. I understand you came in today with nausea and a low-grade fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I woke up feeling queasy, had chills, and my temperature was 99. I called my oncologist and he told me to come in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good call. I see you have two biliary drains—one capped and one that usually drains into a bag. How much output do you normally get?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "About 30 to 40 cc a day from the one on gravity. But today—nothing. I opened the other one too, just in case, and that’s dry as well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s concerning. No output could mean a blockage. You also mentioned some right upper quadrant pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a little, especially when I cough. But it’s not sharp or anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understood. We’ve checked your labs and your bilirubin is elevated. That, plus the fever and no drain output, makes us worry about a biliary obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like last time? But I just finished antibiotics a few weeks ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Given your history of cholangitis and E. coli bacteremia, we’ve started you on IV meropenem just in case. But we need to find out if the tube is blocked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what happens next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get a chest X-ray to make sure there’s no infection in your lungs, and then tomorrow morning, interventional radiology will do a cholangiogram to look at the drain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And if it’s blocked?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-06-11 20:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They may replace the tube. It’s a common procedure for patients like you. We’ll keep you on antibiotics until we know more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-06-12 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your liver enzymes are up—alkaline phosphatase and bilirubin are elevated. That supports the idea of a blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-06-12 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not just in my head. I knew something was off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-06-12 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. The radiology team is reviewing your case now. You’re scheduled for a cholangiogram this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-06-12 10:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mr. Johnson, the procedure is done. They found a blockage in the distal part of your PTBD tube. It was completely obstructed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-06-12 10:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So that’s why nothing was coming out?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-06-12 10:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. They removed the old tube and put in a new 8 French PTBD catheter. It’s now draining into a bag."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-06-12 10:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that the same kind of tube I had before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-06-12 10:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, same type but fresh. The old one likely got clogged with sludge or debris. This should fix the flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-06-12 10:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the antibiotics? Do I still need them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-06-12 10:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re waiting on infectious disease to weigh in. Since your blood cultures are negative and you don’t have signs of active infection, they may stop them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-06-12 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Update: ID agrees. No signs of cholangitis—your fever’s gone, labs are stable. They don’t think you need more antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-06-12 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m off the IV meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-06-12 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll discontinue the meropenem. Your symptoms were likely from the blockage, not an active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-06-12 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried about another round of sepsis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-06-12 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understandable. But you’re not showing signs of that now. Your drain is working, and your liver numbers should start to improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-06-13 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your bilirubin dropped from 1.6 to 0.4 today. That’s a great sign the new tube is doing its job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-06-13 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel better too—no nausea, no pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-06-13 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’re going to cap the drain later today to see if you tolerate it, just like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-06-13 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We capped the PTBD an hour ago. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-06-13 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Fine. No discomfort at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-06-13 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep it capped overnight. If you stay symptom-free, we can discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-06-13 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Home? That’d be nice. But what about the drain care?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-06-13 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Home health will visit you twice a week to check the site and manage the drain. You’ll also have a nurse teach you some basics before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You made it through the night with the drain capped—no issues. We’re clearing you to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Avoid heavy lifting. Keep the site clean and dry. Call us if you develop fever, pain, or the drain stops working again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my oncologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, follow up with him in a week. Your cancer is still being monitored, but no treatment changes now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my platelets? They’ve been low for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your platelet count is 81, which is low but stable for you. No intervention needed unless it drops further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. We’ll send all instructions with you, and home health will be at your house tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. I’ll keep an eye on things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You know your body best. Call us at the first sign of trouble."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, Mr. Johnson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-06-14 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-06-11 20:35:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-06-14 14:25:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. Johnson, a patient with stage IV cholangiocarcinoma and a history of biliary drains, was readmitted with nausea, chills, and absence of biliary drain output. He was initially treated with IV meropenem for suspected cholangitis. A cholangiogram revealed obstruction of the distal PTBD catheter, which was successfully replaced percutaneously. Post-procedure, his symptoms resolved, liver enzymes improved, and blood cultures remained negative. Infectious disease determined antibiotics were unnecessary, as the presentation was consistent with mechanical obstruction rather than infection. The drain was capped without complications, and he was discharged home with home health support for drain care. His thrombocytopenia remained stable, and oncology follow-up was arranged.",
    "problems": [
      "Other mechanical complication of bile duct prosthesis, initial encounter",
      "Obstruction of bile duct",
      "Intrahepatic bile duct carcinoma",
      "Thrombocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Benign prostatic hyperplasia without lower urinary tract symptoms",
      "Migraine, unspecified, not intractable, without status migrainosus"
    ]
  }
}
